---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { hrefOf } from '../lib/nav';

const paths = [
  { when: 'New product, empty folder', run: 'scope → architect → develop → verify → review', why: 'Nothing exists yet, so every decision is still open and cheap to make well.' },
  { when: 'New feature in a live project', run: 'scope (small) → develop → verify → review → sync', why: 'The architecture already exists; the job is fitting in without drifting from it.' },
  { when: 'Code you did not write', run: 'audit → develop → verify → review', why: 'Learning the conventions is the work. The change itself is usually small.' },
  { when: 'Something is broken', run: 'debug → develop (targeted) → verify → review', why: 'Diagnosis first. A fix before a diagnosis is a guess with a commit message.' },
];

const depths = [
  { name: 'Prototype', gets: 'Build only', use: 'Throwaway spikes, experiments you will delete.' },
  { name: 'Alpha', gets: '+ verify it runs', use: 'Internal tools, demos with a real user in the room.' },
  { name: 'Beta', gets: '+ tests', use: 'Anything other people depend on.' },
  { name: 'GA', gets: '+ second-model review and docs', use: 'Money, personal data, auth, anything you cannot quietly revert.' },
];

const prompts = [
  { id: 'scope', title: 'Scope', body: `Challenge this idea before any code. What is genuinely needed for v1, what
should be explicitly out, and what do I not know yet? Push back where I am
assuming something. Write the result to PLAN.md with numbered acceptance
criteria I could test.` },
  { id: 'review', title: 'Review, in a new session', body: `Review this branch's diff against main. You did not write this code.
1. Does it do what the spec says, and nothing the spec excluded?
2. Does it match the contract and this codebase's conventions?
3. Bugs: wrong logic, unhandled errors, data loss, access control.
4. Tests: do any of them assert nothing meaningful?
For each finding: severity, file and line, what breaks, the fix.
Sort into: fix directly / ask me / park. Invent nothing.` },
  { id: 'audit', title: 'Audit an inherited repo', body: `Audit this repository into docs/AUDIT.md. Change no code.
Entry points, one traced request end to end, conventions with quoted
examples, what I must go through rather than around, fragile areas, and
what you could not work out. Cite file paths for everything. If two parts
of the codebase disagree about a convention, show me both.` },
  { id: 'debug', title: 'Debug without guessing', body: `Do not fix anything yet.
1. Reproduce it as a failing test, smallest case you can.
2. Narrow it: where is the data still right, and where is it first wrong?
3. State the root cause in one sentence. If you cannot, say what you would
   need to find out and how you would check it.
4. Only then propose the smallest fix, and what else it could affect.
If at any point you are guessing, say "I am guessing" and stop.` },
  { id: 'sync', title: 'Sync the project memory', body: `The change on this branch just landed. Update the project's memory:
does the contract still match reality, does anything in AGENTS.md now
contradict the code, is any line in it something you could infer from the
code, and what decision did we make that is not written down?
Propose the edits as a diff. Change nothing until I approve.` },
  { id: 'handover', title: 'Rescue a session going in circles', body: `Stop. Do not attempt another fix.
Write HANDOFF.md with five sections: goal, what is known to be true (with
evidence), what has been tried and failed, what is still unknown, and the
single next step. Then I will start a fresh session from that file.` },
];

const commands = [
  { title: 'Sessions and isolation', lines: [
    ['tmux new -s ledger', 'a session per project'],
    ['Ctrl+b d', 'detach; the work keeps running'],
    ['tmux attach -t ledger', 'come back to it'],
    ['claude --worktree feature-x', 'isolated checkout and branch'],
    ['git worktree list', 'see every worktree'],
    ['git worktree remove ../path', 'clean one up'],
  ] },
  { title: 'Inside a session', lines: [
    ['/clear', 'new task, new context'],
    ['/compact', 'same task, running out of room'],
    ['/context', 'what is filling the window'],
    ['/mcp', 'connected servers and their health'],
    ['/agents', 'where your subagent files live'],
    ['/tasks', 'background work in this session'],
  ] },
];
---

<Base
  title="Cheat sheets"
  description="The loop, the four entry points, the prompts worth keeping, and the commands you will actually reach for."
  active="cheatsheets"
>
  <main id="main" class="ref">
    <header class="ref-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Cheat sheets</p>
      <h1>The parts you will look up again</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Everything here is taught properly somewhere in the course. This page exists for the second week, when you know
        what you are doing and just need the wording, the order, or the flag.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="group">
      <h2>Which path to run</h2>
      <p class="group-intro">You rarely run all nine stages. Which ones you run depends on the situation you are in, and there are only four.</p>
      <div class="tbl-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Which path to run">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Situation</th><th>Path</th><th>Why this one</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {paths.map((p) => (<tr><td class="k">{p.when}</td><td class="mono">{p.run}</td><td>{p.why}</td></tr>))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="note">Whichever door you came in by, never skip review. When you are not sure which situation you are in, you are in the audit one.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="group">
      <h2>How much checking a change gets</h2>
      <p class="group-intro">Depth is a decision, not a mood. Pick it when you pick the task, and write the project's default in WORKFLOW.md.</p>
      <div class="tbl-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="How much checking a change gets">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Depth</th><th>What it adds</th><th>Use it for</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {depths.map((d) => (<tr><td class="k">{d.name}</td><td class="mono">{d.gets}</td><td>{d.use}</td></tr>))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="group">
      <h2>Prompts worth keeping</h2>
      <p class="group-intro">Copy these, then adapt the wording to your project. The structure is what matters: an outcome, the boundaries, and what counts as proof.</p>
      <div class="sheets">
        {prompts.map((p) => (
          <figure class="sheet">
            <figcaption>{p.title}<button class="copy" type="button" data-copy={p.id}>Copy</button></figcaption>
            <pre id={`p-${p.id}`}>{p.body}</pre>
          </figure>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="group">
      <h2>Commands</h2>
      <div class="cmds">
        {commands.map((c) => (
          <div class="cmd-card">
            <h3>{c.title}</h3>
            <dl>
              {c.lines.map(([cmd, what]) => (<div><dt><code>{cmd}</code></dt><dd>{what}</dd></div>))}
            </dl>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="group">
      <h2>Guardrails worth having everywhere</h2>
      <p class="group-intro">Five minutes, once per project. Built in <a href={hrefOf('p1/guardrails')}>Guardrails</a>, and included in your kit.</p>
      <figure class="sheet">
        <figcaption>.claude/settings.json<button class="copy" type="button" data-copy="guard">Copy</button></figcaption>
        <pre id="p-guard">{`"permissions": {
  "deny": [
    "Read(./.env)", "Read(./.env.*)",
    "Bash(rm -rf *)", "Bash(git push --force *)",
    "Bash(git commit --no-verify *)", "Bash(git push --no-verify *)"
  ],
  "ask": ["Bash(git push *)"]
}`}</pre>
      </figure>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  .ref { max-width: 1060px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 56px 22px 100px; }
  .ref-head { max-width: 72ch; }
  .eyebrow { font: 700 0.76rem var(--font-mono); letter-spacing: 0.13em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent-strong); margin-bottom: 12px; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 5vw, 3.2rem); font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.035em; margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .lede { font-size: 1.12rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .group { margin-top: 52px; }
  .group h2 { font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 3vw, 1.85rem); font-weight: 750; letter-spacing: -0.025em; margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .group-intro { color: var(--ink-soft); max-width: 68ch; margin-bottom: 20px; }

  .tbl-wrap:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 2px; }
  .tbl-wrap { overflow-x: auto; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius-l); background: var(--surface); }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; min-width: 680px; font-size: 0.94rem; }
  th { text-align: left; font: 700 0.68rem var(--font-mono); letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-faint); padding: 12px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  td { padding: 13px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); vertical-align: top; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  tr:last-child td { border-bottom: 0; }
  td.k { font-weight: 650; color: var(--ink); }
  td.mono { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--ink); }

  .sheets { display: grid; gap: 18px; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(360px, 1fr)); }
  .sheet { margin: 0; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius-l); overflow: hidden; background: var(--code-bg); }
  .sheet figcaption {
    display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 10px;
    font: 600 0.8rem var(--font-mono); color: var(--code-dim);
    padding: 10px 14px; background: var(--code-bar);
  }
  .sheet pre { margin: 0; padding: 14px 16px; font: 400 0.83rem/1.6 var(--font-mono); color: var(--code-ink); background: var(--code-bg); white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .copy { font: 600 0.72rem var(--font-mono); color: var(--code-dim); background: transparent; border: 1px solid var(--code-dim); border-radius: 7px; padding: 4px 9px; cursor: pointer; }
  .copy:hover { color: var(--code-ink); border-color: var(--code-ink); }

  .cmds { display: grid; gap: 18px; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(320px, 1fr)); }
  .cmd-card { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius-l); padding: 18px 20px; }
  .cmd-card h3 { font: 750 1.05rem var(--font-display); margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .cmd-card dl { margin: 0; display: grid; gap: 8px; }
  .cmd-card dl > div { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(120px, auto) 1fr; gap: 12px; align-items: baseline; }
  .cmd-card dt code { font-size: 0.82rem; }
  .cmd-card dd { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 0.88rem; }
  @media (max-width: 560px) { .ref { padding-top: 36px; } .cmd-card dl > div { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 2px; } }
</style>

<script is:inline>
  document.querySelectorAll('[data-copy]').forEach(function (btn) {
    btn.addEventListener('click', function () {
      var pre = document.getElementById('p-' + btn.getAttribute('data-copy'));
      if (!pre) return;
      navigator.clipboard.writeText(pre.textContent || '').then(function () {
        var old = btn.textContent;
        btn.textContent = 'Copied';
        setTimeout(function () { btn.textContent = old; }, 1400);
      }).catch(function () { btn.textContent = 'Press ⌘C'; });
    });
  });
</script>
